      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "They need to disallow world asset editing, people can crash a whole world regardless of safety settings. Theres also a viewpoint crasher that gives you infinite viewpoints. People can edit the world in an instance then they take all the objects and expand them to the maximum all at the same time or sometimes they just remove all the colliders in the world. I try to report crashers consistently I also made a support ticket on this topic I would copy paste my support ticket but i don’t have access to it. Also i heard that people can grab ip addresses through video players. Maybe a cheat report section would be nice. Anticheat/security needs a step up. Cheaters and crashers usually do what they do as an act of discrimination I see this as a pretty big problem and it compromises the social environment.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-14T15:25:30.366Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's beyond ridiculous when you can't feel safe even with safety settings on. Even just having 'avatar' on in safety with no shaders/effects can still get you crashed if the person has a standard shader crasher. Client users ram lag entire worlds because they've got nothing better to do and people who actually care about the game are the ones suffering.\nPeople are only going to put up with this for so long before giving up on this game, you know.",
